From: smit1237 <smit1237@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 05:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] LXMRouter: re-date state recorded before the clock was set

RNSBox runs lxmd / nomadnet as propagation nodes whether or not the wall
clock is set: with no RTC and no NTP (HaLow-, LAN- or WiFi-only meshes) the
clock starts at 1970, or ~2000 on an unset DS3231. Timestamps LXMRouter
takes then look decades old once the clock is set (NTP, a browser sync, a
later trusted-RTC boot), and its wall-clock expiry drops the state:

 - Stored messages are named <transient_id>_<received>_<stamp> with that
   received time; clean_message_store() (every 8 min on a propagation node)
   purges an entry once now > received + MESSAGE_EXPIRY, so the first clean
   after the clock is set deletes every message stored while it was unset.
 - peer() and a successful sync set a propagation peer's last_heard to the
   local clock; sync_peers() (every 24 s) culls a peer once now > last_heard
   + LXMPeer.MAX_UNREACHABLE (14 d), so every peer heard while the clock was
   unset is dropped as unreachable, with the unhandled-message lists that
   are rebuilt from self.peers when the store is saved.
 - clean_transient_id_caches() purges locally delivered / processed
   transient IDs past MESSAGE_EXPIRY*6, so messages already handled while
   the clock was unset could be accepted and delivered again.

Instead, when such a timestamp is below CLOCK_FLOOR (2020-01-01 UTC, the
floor RNSBox's S45ntpsync and portal use for a plausible clock) and the
clock now reads at or above it, re-date it to the current time:

 - a stored message's file is renamed with the current time and the entry's
   path and receive time updated, so it gets its full 30-day lifetime from
   when the clock was set (updating entry[2] also keeps get_weight()'s
   storage-limit culling from treating it as decades old);
 - a peer's last_heard is set to now (one never heard, at 0, is left
   alone: the startup path-request logic keys on that), so only a peer
   genuinely unheard for 14 days is culled;
 - a transient-ID cache entry is re-stamped with now instead of purged.

While the clock is still unset, everything works on the unset clock as
before.

Signed-off-by: smit1237 <smit1237@gmail.com>
---
 LXMF/LXMRouter.py | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/LXMF/LXMRouter.py b/LXMF/LXMRouter.py
--- a/LXMF/LXMRouter.py
+++ b/LXMF/LXMRouter.py
@@ -36,6 +36,10 @@
     P_LINK_MAX_INACTIVITY = 3*60
 
     MESSAGE_EXPIRY        = 30*24*60*60
+    # RNSBox: a receive timestamp below this (2020-01-01 UTC) was taken while
+    # the wall clock was unset (no RTC / no NTP yet: 1970, ~2000 on an unset
+    # DS3231). Re-dated once the clock is set instead of expired or culled.
+    CLOCK_FLOOR           = 1577836800
     STAMP_COST_EXPIRY     = 45*24*60*60
 
     NODE_ANNOUNCE_DELAY   = 20
@@ -958,7 +962,11 @@
         removed_entries = []
         for transient_id in self.locally_delivered_transient_ids:
             timestamp = self.locally_delivered_transient_ids[transient_id]
-            if now > timestamp+LXMRouter.MESSAGE_EXPIRY*6.0:
+            if timestamp < LXMRouter.CLOCK_FLOOR <= now:
+                # RNSBox: recorded while the clock was unset; keep it
+                # (re-dated) so the message isn't accepted again.
+                self.locally_delivered_transient_ids[transient_id] = now
+            elif now > timestamp+LXMRouter.MESSAGE_EXPIRY*6.0:
                 removed_entries.append(transient_id)
 
         for transient_id in removed_entries:
@@ -968,7 +976,9 @@
         removed_entries = []
         for transient_id in self.locally_processed_transient_ids:
             timestamp = self.locally_processed_transient_ids[transient_id]
-            if now > timestamp+LXMRouter.MESSAGE_EXPIRY*6.0:
+            if timestamp < LXMRouter.CLOCK_FLOOR <= now:
+                self.locally_processed_transient_ids[transient_id] = now
+            elif now > timestamp+LXMRouter.MESSAGE_EXPIRY*6.0:
                 removed_entries.append(transient_id)
 
         for transient_id in removed_entries:
@@ -1106,7 +1116,18 @@
 
             if len(components) == 3 and float(components[1]) > 0 and len(os.path.split(components[0])[1]) == (RNS.Identity.HASHLENGTH//8)*2 and int(components[2]) == stamp_value:
                 timestamp = float(components[1])
-                if now > timestamp+LXMRouter.MESSAGE_EXPIRY:
+                if timestamp < LXMRouter.CLOCK_FLOOR <= now:
+                    # Stored before the clock was set: give it its full expiry
+                    # from now rather than purging it as decades old.
+                    new_path = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(filepath), f"{components[0]}_{now}_{components[2]}")
+                    try:
+                        os.rename(filepath, new_path)
+                        entry[1] = new_path
+                        entry[2] = now
+                        RNS.log("Re-dated message "+RNS.prettyhexrep(transient_id)+" stored before the clock was set", RNS.LOG_DEBUG)
+                    except Exception as e:
+                        RNS.log("Could not re-date "+RNS.prettyhexrep(transient_id)+" in the message store. The contained exception was: "+str(e), RNS.LOG_ERROR)
+                elif now > timestamp+LXMRouter.MESSAGE_EXPIRY:
                     RNS.log("Purging message "+RNS.prettyhexrep(transient_id)+" due to expiry", RNS.LOG_EXTREME)
                     removed_entries[transient_id] = filepath
             else:
@@ -2029,8 +2050,13 @@
         waiting_peers = []
         unresponsive_peers = []
         peers = self.peers.copy()
+        now = time.time()
         for peer_id in peers:
             peer = peers[peer_id]
+            if 0 < peer.last_heard < LXMRouter.CLOCK_FLOOR <= now:
+                # RNSBox: heard while the clock was unset. Re-date it rather
+                # than cull the peer as unreachable for decades.
+                peer.last_heard = now
             if time.time() > peer.last_heard + LXMPeer.MAX_UNREACHABLE:
                 if not peer_id in self.static_peers: culled_peers.append(peer_id)
             
-- 
